<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  pwa-pantry-recipes.example.plist — the LaunchAgent template for the Pantry
  Recipes PWA.

  *** THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE. IT MUST NOT BE INSTALLED WITHOUT EXPLICIT
      AUTHORIZATION FROM THE USER IN THE SAME SESSION. ***

  AGENTS.md records deployment as not yet authorized, and
  docs/runbook/deployment.md is the plan. Prepare it with
  scripts/install_launchagent.sh, never by hand: the two settings that break
  silently (the file-descriptor ceiling and the log directory's parent) are
  both invisible in a plist that merely parses.

  Two ports, never one end-to-end
    8007  this process. A loopback bind, and the only thing it listens on.
    8452  the Tailscale Serve ingress the phone reaches. Tailscale proxies
          8452 to 127.0.0.1:8007. Never 443; 8000/8002-8006 and 8443-8451 are
          allocated to sibling PWAs. See docs/runbook/deployment.md.

  Invariants
    * BIND_HOST MUST be loopback (127.0.0.1). app/config.py refuses a
      non-loopback bind in every mode, and with TRUST_TAILSCALE_HEADERS=true it
      refuses at startup with trusted_headers_require_loopback_bind. The
      Tailscale Serve proxy, not this process, is the only network-facing
      surface. If you ever change the bind host you are no longer deploying
      this topology; re-read the runbook first.
    * TRUST_TAILSCALE_HEADERS=true means the app trusts the Tailscale-User-Login
      header ONLY because the connection arrived from the proxy over loopback.
      With it false, app/auth.py is in development-identity mode: it REJECTS any
      client-supplied Tailscale header with 401 identity_spoof and answers as
      DEV_IDENTITY. The value below is the production posture, and it is only
      correct once the Serve route on 8452 exists and carries the owner login.
    * The server-owned roots (PANTRY_ITEMS_DB, PANTRY_NOTE_RELATIVE,
      RECIPES_ROOT, DAILY_NOTES_ROOT) are set here and are NOT overridable by any
      request. No request field reaches Settings.

  THE ENVIRONMENT MECHANISM
    This app has NO .env parser. Settings.from_environment() reads os.environ,
    full stop. So the EnvironmentVariables dict below IS the mechanism, and it
    is the shape every sibling agent on this machine runs
    (com.syang.pwa-obsidian-daily.plist is the same). The "set -a; . ./.env;
    set +a" incantation in README.md is how a SHELL picks the same values up for
    a dev server; it has no effect here, because launchd does not run a shell.
    Copying .env.example to .env therefore configures nothing and must never be
    mistaken for having done so. Every value below is validated at boot, and a
    bad one refuses startup rather than degrading to an empty result.

  PERMISSIONS
    APP_DATA_DIR must be mode 0700. install_launchagent.sh creates it with
    "install -d -m 700". It does not touch a .env file, because this dict is the
    mechanism and a second source of truth for the same values is how they
    drift.

  Replace every __UPPER_CASE__ placeholder below, then run
  scripts/install_launchagent.sh. Its three stages are: render and lint (no
  authorization, no side effects), apply (creates APP_DATA_DIR and the log
  directory, copies the plist, starts NOTHING), and bootstrap (bootout then
  bootstrap — the step that starts a service which writes cooking logs into the
  real vault, and the reason the other two stages exist).

  A plist edit needs bootout followed by bootstrap. A kickstart re-reads the
  binary and IGNORES the plist, so a NumberOfFiles fix that is only kickedstart
  leaves the old settings running and reports success. A code-only change needs
  kickstart -k. Never the force flag.

  Then prove the socket rather than the process (port_manager.py inspect 8007)
  and run the converge gate (scripts/converge_gate.py) against both the local
  and the deployed origin. A restart is not a release: launchctl print showing
  state = running proves a process is alive, and a matching /api/version proves
  the frontend is current. Neither proves the backend reloaded configuration —
  that is the gate's condition 3.

  Unload and rollback: bootout the label, then remove the plist from
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents. install_launchagent.sh has a teardown mode for it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Must match the filename in ~/Library/LaunchAgents. -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.syang.pwa-pantry-recipes</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <!-- Absolute python from the project venv. -->
        <string>__VENV_DIR__/bin/python</string>
        <string>-m</string>
        <string>uvicorn</string>
        <!-- The factory reads the environment at boot, not at import. -->
        <string>app.main:create_app</string>
        <string>--factory</string>
        <!-- Loopback only. Never 0.0.0.0. -->
        <string>--host</string>
        <string>127.0.0.1</string>
        <!-- Dedicated app port 8007 (8000/8002-8006 allocated to sibling
             PWAs: wardrobe prod/dev, deals, obsidian-daily, obsidian-monthly,
             obsidian-editor). Not 443, and not the Serve ingress port. -->
        <string>--port</string>
        <string>8007</string>
        <string>--log-level</string>
        <string>info</string>
        <!-- A vault write is in flight-dated work: a 5 s grace lets the atomic
             write finish, and makes KeepAlive's respawn predictable instead of
             racing a half-closed AtomicNoteStore. -->
        <string>--timeout-graceful-shutdown</string>
        <string>5</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>__REPO_ROOT__</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <!-- Exact PATH the daemon needs: the venv bin plus the system dirs, so
             python/uvicorn resolve without a login shell. -->
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>__VENV_DIR__/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>__USER_HOME__</string>

        <!-- === Core (required; a bad value refuses startup) === -->
        <key>OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH</key>
        <string>__OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH__</string>
        <!-- Must be OUTSIDE the vault, and mode 0700. -->
        <key>APP_DATA_DIR</key>
        <string>__APP_DATA_DIR__</string>
        <!-- Must equal the exact origin Tailscale Serve serves, byte for byte:
             scheme, host and port, no path, no trailing slash. The Origin guard
             compares mutations against it exactly, so one extra slash here is
             every mutation answered 403 origin_not_allowed. -->
        <key>PUBLIC_ORIGIN</key>
        <string>__PUBLIC_ORIGIN__</string>
        <!-- Must equal the normalized login the proxy injects, byte for byte. -->
        <key>TAILSCALE_OWNER_LOGIN</key>
        <string>__TAILSCALE_OWNER_LOGIN__</string>
        <!-- Only used when TRUST_TAILSCALE_HEADERS is false. -->
        <key>DEV_IDENTITY</key>
        <string>__DEV_IDENTITY__</string>
        <key>BIND_HOST</key>
        <string>127.0.0.1</string>
        <!-- true ONLY behind the loopback Tailscale Serve proxy. -->
        <key>TRUST_TAILSCALE_HEADERS</key>
        <string>true</string>
        <key>APP_TIMEZONE</key>
        <string>America/New_York</string>

        <!-- === Server-owned domain roots (no request field reaches these) === -->
        <!-- wholefoods-to-pantry's SQLite catalog (`items`). Opened READ-ONLY by
             this app; that project remains the sole writer. Must be OUTSIDE the
             vault. A missing file refuses startup, so a bad path can never look
             like an empty pantry. -->
        <key>PANTRY_ITEMS_DB</key>
        <string>__PANTRY_ITEMS_DB__</string>
        <!-- The live Pantry.md: Pantry Stock state (open/in_progress/done/cancelled,
             per Pantry Unit). Read-only to this app. The catalog above says what
             is bought; this says what is held now (F1). -->
        <key>PANTRY_NOTE_RELATIVE</key>
        <string>__PANTRY_NOTE_RELATIVE__</string>
        <!-- Vault-relative folder of recipe notes. Read-only to this app. -->
        <key>RECIPES_ROOT</key>
        <string>__RECIPES_ROOT__</string>
        <!-- Vault-relative root of year-subfoldered daily notes; a cooking log
             is appended to the dated note inside it. Nothing here ever creates a
             missing daily note (F4): that is a 404 naming the date, not a write. -->
        <key>DAILY_NOTES_ROOT</key>
        <string>__DAILY_NOTES_ROOT__</string>
        <!-- Empty means the daily notes' own layout is the only bound on the
             year. A value must be YYYY-YYYY, e.g. 2024-2027. -->
        <key>DAILY_NOTES_YEAR_POLICY</key>
        <string>__DAILY_NOTES_YEAR_POLICY__</string>

        <!-- === Write posture and read budgets === -->
        <!-- true refuses EVERY /api/* mutation with 403 read_only, after identity
             and before every other mutation check. There is deliberately no write
             allowlist (F18): with F4 removing the note-creation service this flag
             is the only gate between a mutation and the vault. Start read-only
             (docs/runbook/deployment.md § 6). -->
        <key>OBSIDIAN_READ_ONLY</key>
        <string>__OBSIDIAN_READ_ONLY__</string>
        <!-- F11. STOCK_CACHE_SECONDS is the maximum staleness a chip colour can
             have, because the user toggles Pantry.md lines from Obsidian with
             this PWA open. -->
        <key>CATALOG_CACHE_SECONDS</key>
        <string>300</string>
        <key>STOCK_CACHE_SECONDS</key>
        <string>30</string>
        <key>RECIPE_CACHE_SECONDS</key>
        <string>60</string>
        <!-- Hard ceiling on the bytes read from one note, so a runaway or
             hostile file is refused before it is parsed. -->
        <key>MAX_RECIPE_BYTES</key>
        <string>2000000</string>
        <!-- Hours after it was written that a Cooking Record may be retracted
             from the PWA. Past this it is history, edited in Obsidian. -->
        <key>COOK_LOG_UNDO_HOURS</key>
        <string>72</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- Keep the loopback server alive; restart on crash. -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Space out respawns so a crash loop cannot spin the CPU. -->
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>2</integer>
    <!-- RunAtLoad starts it at login. Remove this key during a staged rollout so
         a reboot cannot bring up a configuration that has not been validated. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- launchd gives a LaunchAgent a 256 maxfiles soft limit, NOT the shell's
         `ulimit -n`. This is NOT optional in this app: `AtomicNoteStore` holds
         pinned directory descriptors for the lifetime of the process by design,
         and the lifespan's `finally` is the only thing that releases them. At
         256 the app dies under a load the shell never notices. The key only
         raises the ceiling; it does not excuse a leak, and
         scripts/converge_gate.py does not check for one; count them with lsof against the
         pid after a burst instead. -->
    <key>SoftResourceLimits</key>
    <dict>
        <key>NumberOfFiles</key>
        <integer>8192</integer>
    </dict>

    <!-- Under ~/Library/Logs, the convention every sibling agent on this machine
         uses. NOT a path inside the repo: launchd creates the log FILES but never
         their parent directory, so a `__REPO_ROOT__/logs/...` path fails to spawn
         with no error the operator can see — the job simply never starts. The
         installer `mkdir -p`s this directory. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__USER_HOME__/Library/Logs/pwa-pantry-recipes/server.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__USER_HOME__/Library/Logs/pwa-pantry-recipes/server.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
